[SPEAKER_05]: Unless you fully abandon sensuality beforehand, it's not possible to enter jhāna, to experience jhāna.

375
00:24:44,958 --> 00:24:49,041
[SPEAKER_05]: And in other suttas it says that the first jhāna is necessary for fruits of anāgāmī.

376
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:53,883
[SPEAKER_05]: In other words, anāgāmī is free from sensuality before he's an anāgāmī.

377
00:24:54,544 --> 00:24:58,367
[SPEAKER_05]: That's why he's an anāgāmī, because he's free from sensuality, not other way around.

378
00:25:00,289 --> 00:25:02,350
[SPEAKER_02]: So, this is a fifth amazing quality.

379
00:25:03,371 --> 00:25:09,776
[SPEAKER_02]: Ever since I declared myself a lay follower, I can't recall deliberately breaking any precepts.

380
00:25:12,939 --> 00:25:13,179
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

381
00:25:13,579 --> 00:25:14,160
[SPEAKER_02]: So, when she

382
00:25:16,053 --> 00:25:16,673
[SPEAKER_02]: Declared.

383
00:25:17,734 --> 00:25:19,575
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, by the way, yeah, I am a lay follower.

384
00:25:19,595 --> 00:25:22,816
[SPEAKER_05]: When she understood dhamma, she got the right view.

385
00:25:23,016 --> 00:25:24,397
[SPEAKER_02]: For the rest of my life.

386
00:25:24,417 --> 00:25:28,019
[SPEAKER_05]: Yeah, that's usually when people declare being a lay follower means they understood the dhamma.

387
00:25:28,939 --> 00:25:29,660
[SPEAKER_05]: As a householder.

388
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:31,641
[SPEAKER_02]: And hers.

389
00:25:32,461 --> 00:25:33,161
[SPEAKER_05]: And then jhānas.

390
00:25:33,702 --> 00:25:37,804
[SPEAKER_02]: Six, yeah, her six amazing qualities that she can get all jhānas at will.

391
00:25:38,524 --> 00:25:38,724
[SPEAKER_05]: Yeah.

392
00:25:40,477 --> 00:25:48,821
[SPEAKER_02]: And then the seventh was, eh... of the five lower fetters taught by the Buddha, I don't see any that I haven't given up.

393
00:25:50,542 --> 00:25:51,603
[SPEAKER_05]: See, that's another thing.

394
00:25:51,943 --> 00:25:52,684
[SPEAKER_05]: Given up.

395
00:25:54,364 --> 00:25:58,767
[SPEAKER_05]: It's something you maintain, you hold on to, and you see that, you know that.

396
00:25:59,597 --> 00:26:02,378
[SPEAKER_05]: And that's those little things that I keep saying throughout the day.

397
00:26:02,958 --> 00:26:04,399
[SPEAKER_05]: Little thoughts, little actions.

398
00:26:04,859 --> 00:26:06,759
[SPEAKER_05]: That is... that is your... your tether.

399
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:08,180
[SPEAKER_05]: That is your connection to it.

400
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:13,662
[SPEAKER_05]: That you're willingly, at every individual instance, refusing to give up.

401
00:26:15,182 --> 00:26:16,723
[SPEAKER_04]: Because you're not diligent enough.

402
00:26:16,763 --> 00:26:17,263
[SPEAKER_05]: Simple as that.

403
00:26:17,843 --> 00:26:28,507
[SPEAKER_05]: So, the diligence is measured then on that level, not on how many hours per day you stay awake and sleep, and how many... how many meditation sessions you have, and how

404
00:26:28,900 --> 00:26:32,162
[SPEAKER_05]: How silent you are, how slow you walk and... No.

405
00:26:32,382 --> 00:26:39,547
[SPEAKER_05]: It's how diligent you are in regard to dispelling the unwholesome states and purifying thoughts as they arise, enduring them on the right level and not acting out of it.

406
00:26:41,568 --> 00:26:43,109
[SPEAKER_05]: So, she given them up.

407
00:26:44,150 --> 00:26:44,490
[SPEAKER_05]: Fully.

408
00:26:45,030 --> 00:26:48,273
[SPEAKER_05]: She can't see anything that she hasn't given up in terms of the five lower factors.

409
00:26:50,054 --> 00:26:51,875
[SPEAKER_05]: So, how do you abandon the five lower factors?

410
00:26:51,975 --> 00:26:52,735
[SPEAKER_05]: By giving them up.

411
00:26:53,456 --> 00:26:54,937
[SPEAKER_05]: Everything that partakes in them.

412
00:27:04,212 --> 00:27:04,692
[SPEAKER_02]: The choice.

413
00:27:05,853 --> 00:27:06,954
[SPEAKER_02]: When you can see your choice.

414
00:27:06,974 --> 00:27:07,294
[SPEAKER_05]: Exactly.

415
00:27:08,015 --> 00:27:18,002
[SPEAKER_05]: And you, once you're basically restrained enough, having kept the precepts enough, so you stop ignoring your choice, because automatically you ignore the choice.

416
00:27:18,222 --> 00:27:19,103
[SPEAKER_05]: The choice is always there.

417
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:20,484
[SPEAKER_05]: You see that.

418
00:27:20,564 --> 00:27:22,045
[SPEAKER_05]: Take, to touch, to look, to hear.

419
00:27:22,566 --> 00:27:27,669
[SPEAKER_05]: You just ignore it, because it's just too quick, too small, too little, too insignificant, seemingly, so...

420
00:27:29,808 --> 00:27:39,154
[SPEAKER_05]: Well, if you are basically not ignoring that choice, the choice becomes apparent and that's how you purify it in its arising, which is an amazing quality.

